# Constraint Enforcement

Hard constraints from `docs/spec.md` §Constraints & Assumptions and standing ADRs.
Violations are blocking — do not proceed without raising a `[Decision]`.

[Corpus: system-spec] [Corpus: config] [Corpus: deps]

## Version Pins

| Dependency | Required Version | Source |
|------------|------------------|--------|
| Python | **3.11** (`>=3.11,<3.12`) | spec H10; `pyproject.toml` |
| Node | **24 LTS** | spec H10; dependency-inventory |
| Modal SDK | per `docs/dependency-inventory.md` | deps |

Do not upgrade language pins without an ADR / decision. GPU stack pins for Modal LLM /
embed / FT images live in `infra/modal/` and dependency-inventory — change via ADR.

## Platform Constraints

- **Hybrid deploy**: DigitalOcean (HTTP + Postgres) + Modal (embed, LLM, DM workers, FT);
  US regions (spec H2).
- **`DATABASE_URL` only on DO backends** — Modal must not hold the corpus DB URL
  (ADR-007 / H8).
- **`packages/` must not import `apps/`** (ADR-012 / H9).
- Corpus DB holds **no personal account/session/message tables** (H5); admin identity
  is Supabase-only (ADR-026).

## Excluded / gated patterns

| Pattern | Rule |
|---------|------|
| Live prod corpus mutate / FT promote / automation enable | AskQuestion required ([no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc](no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc)) |
| Operator DO spec exports (`*-spec.yaml` with secrets) | Never commit ([no-operator-spec-commits.mdc](no-operator-spec-commits.mdc)) |
| Paid third-party LLM/embed as default | Forbidden (H6) |
| Antibody Job-template (`cognichem-rfantibody`, `src/rfdiffusion_stage.py`) | Not this product — do not reintroduce |
| Auto-promote LoRA to prod `vecinita-llm` | Forbidden (F77 / ADR-053) |

## Validation Constraints

From `docs/config-spec.md` §Validation Rules — enforce documented bounds in code (e.g.
`top_k`, chunk size/overlap, freshness stale days, FT concurrency/daily caps). Do not
invent alternate defaults without RD/ADR.

## When a Constraint Must Change

If a constraint needs to be relaxed or modified:
1. Raise `[Decision]` citing the constraint and why it needs to change
2. On approval, update this rule and the relevant spec document
3. Create or amend an ADR documenting the change
